# Git Commit Messages (Awesome-adapted · gated)

Use only when the user asks to commit, write a commit message, or prepare a PR title from changes.

## Format
```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer]
```

## Types (common)
- `feat` — new feature / web part behavior
- `fix` — bug fix
- `refactor` — behavior-preserving restructure
- `perf` — performance
- `test` — tests only
- `docs` — docs/comments for humans
- `chore` — tooling, scripts, cursor rules (no user-facing change)
- `build` — Heft/package-solution/manifest build pipeline

## Scope examples
`(trcHome)`, `(complianceTower)`, `(spfx)`, `(cms)` — optional, lowercase inside parens

## Rules
- Imperative, concise subject (~72 chars)
- Body explains **why** when not obvious from diff
- `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer or `type!:` when manifest/API breaks
- Match recent repo commit tone (`git log -5` before drafting)
- Never commit secrets, `.env`, or tenant credentials

## Reject
- Wall-of-text RFC paste in commit body
- Commits without user explicit ask (see user git safety rules)
